<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_disruption" target="energy_market_shift::capital_flow_oil" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Damage to ports, pipelines and transit corridors in the Black Sea/adjacent export routes constrains supply reliability for region-linked crude, increasing returns to non-conflict upstream projects and causing investors to reallocate capital toward alternative oil developments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_disruption" target="energy_market_shift::expropriation_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Severe and sustained disruption of fuel and oil transport infrastructure prompts host governments to impose emergency controls, relicense operations, or seize facilities to secure domestic supply, raising the probability of regulatory expropriation of foreign energy assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_disruption" target="global_financial_tension::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.66</data>
  <data key="d37">Widespread damage to ports and transport nodes strains cash flows and credit in trade-exposed corporates and dealer inventories, causing market makers to pull back and bid-ask spreads to widen, reducing bond-market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_disruption" target="iran_war_stalemate::shipping_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Damage to Black Sea logistics and port nodes diverts cargo onto longer routes and through regional chokepoints (e.g., Suez, Strait of Hormuz), increasing congestion, insurance costs and the probability of maritime incidents in the same corridors used around Iran.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_war_stalemate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_disruption" target="us_china_rivalry::chip_production_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Damage and closure of Black Sea ports and overland logistics chokepoints increase shipping times, insurance costs and shortages for specialty gases, substrates and other inputs that flow through those routes, causing affected fabs to curtail runs and temporarily reduce chip production capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
