  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp spikes in global staple and energy prices driven by the conflict intensify competition among major powers for secure supplies and open markets, prompting more aggressive trade diplomacy, resource-linked alignments, and public confrontation that raise US–China geopolitical tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
