<edge source="global_financial_tension::portfolio_realloc_rate" target="energy_market_shift::asset_transfer_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A faster pace of investor reallocations toward commodity exposure or resource equities increases demand for direct ownership of oil assets and drives more M&amp;A, joint-venture deals and formal asset transfers in the upstream sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_market_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::portfolio_realloc_rate" target="iran_war_stalemate::finance_rerouting" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">When investors rapidly reallocate away from region- or sanction-exposed assets, banks and intermediaries curtail correspondent relationships and payment services for those clients, forcing corporates and banks to route transactions through alternative channels, currencies, or non‑standard intermediaries.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_war_stalemate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::portfolio_realloc_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::commodity_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid portfolio reallocation into commodity futures and physical agricultural hedges (flight to hard assets) increases speculative and physical demand for grains/oilseeds, pushing up spot and futures prices within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::portfolio_realloc_rate" target="us_china_rivalry::chip_production_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid investor reallocation away from capital‑intensive and illiquid tech assets reduces available equity and growth capital for chipmakers and fabs, slowing project financing, construction starts and near‑term capacity additions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
