<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="global_financial_tension::short_term_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened sanction pressure restricts correspondent banking and dollar-clearing relationships for targeted counterparties, shrinking short-term funding supply and forcing banks to raise overnight and short-term lending rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="iran_war_stalemate::finance_rerouting" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened sanctions on energy transactions prompt banks, traders and states to shift payments into alternative currencies, correspondent banks and opaque intermediaries to preserve oil trade.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_war_stalemate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="iran_war_stalemate::domestic_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased sanction pressure on the energy sector directly reduces export receipts and curtails imports of critical goods, producing inflation, shortages and protests that raise domestic political pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_war_stalemate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tightened international energy sanctions curtail Russian oil and gas export volumes and access to payment/finance channels, materially reducing budgetary revenue available for arms procurement, mobilization and sustainment of operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::export_throughput_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalated energy-related sanctions targeting shipping, insurance and port services raises transit risk and rerouting costs in the Black Sea and adjacent corridors, causing delays and reduced volumes of Ukrainian agricultural exports reaching global markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="us_china_rivalry::geopolitical_tension_lev" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">New or intensified sanctions on energy transactions produce immediate diplomatic retaliation, alliance shifts and military signaling between Washington and Beijing (and their partners), raising measured interstate tension.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::sanction_pressure" target="us_china_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Expanding sanction regimes create legal frameworks and domestic political momentum that are translated into stricter, more broadly enforced semiconductor export controls to limit strategic transfers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
