<edge source="energy_market_shift::capital_flow_oil" target="global_financial_tension::portfolio_realloc_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid increase or retrenchment of capital into the oil sector compels institutional investors to rotate allocations (selling or buying other asset classes) to rebalance exposures, raising the observable pace of portfolio reallocation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::capital_flow_oil" target="iran_war_stalemate::economic_warfare" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A surge in foreign capital into a sanctioned jurisdiction's oil sector provokes reciprocal coercive measures (targeted sanctions, asset freezes, trade restrictions) by adversaries seeking to block or punish those investments.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_war_stalemate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_market_shift::capital_flow_oil" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained increase in upstream oil investment raises near- to mid-term global supply expectations and downward pressure on oil prices, lowering Russia's export receipts and therefore its fiscal capacity to finance high-intensity military operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_market_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
